MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

>
> (1) Assuming I've verified there are no significant genotype X year interactions - Would it be correct to combine the phenotype results into one large cross file with the year as covariate (same genotype would appear 3 times next to its result)?
>

This won't work properly. You need to either take averages across the years or use a mixed model to account for the within-line correlations, though the latter is not something you can do in R/qtl.

> (2) I've noticed in the summary of fitqtl that the LOD score of the first qtl step in `stepwiseqtl` (8...@67.9 - LOD 33.7) is much larger than when building the model manually with scanone and addqtl. Is this correct?
>

 The first step of stepwiseqtl is to run either scanone() or addqtl(), and so the results of the first step should be identical.

karl

