MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

R/qtl doesn’t include anything specific for F3 lines. Treating them as RIL would mean omitting all heterozygous genotypes, which I wouldn’t recommend. I think the best you can do, in R/qtl, is to just treat them like an F2.

But there seems to be something wrong, as you mention 7065 markers but the output of read.cross says 7064 individuals but 192 markers. Maybe use format=“csvr”.

karl

